      "part_type": "Hadith",
      "path": "/books/al-kafi:6:6:28:6",
      "text": [
        " أَجِبْ فِي الْوَلِيمَةِ وَ الْخِتَانِ وَ لَا تُجِبْ فِي خَفْضِ الْجَوَارِي ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "Ali Bin Ibrahim, from his father, from Al Nowfaly, from Al Sakuny, ",
          "(It has been narrated) from Abu Abdullah<sup>asws</sup> having said: ‘Answer (to an invitation for a meal) regarding the wedding feast, and the circumcision, and do not answer regarding the female circumcision’."
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          "6. Ali ibn Ibrahim has narrated from his father from al-Nawfaliy from al-Sakuniy who has said the following: “Abu ‘Abd Allah, ‘Alayhi al-Salam, has said, ‘Accept an invitation for a wedding and circumcision; but do not accept for Khafd (lowering) girls.’” "
        ]
      }
    },
